Maybe it depends on the system, but I've never been able to get
restore
to work one tiny bit on the Macintosh. I use the carbon port, which is
probably unwise since it seems to have some fatal bugs on OS X. So
count me in as another vote that keeping a single backup in case of
crash isn't cheating.

Restoring a save after a crash can have some gameplay effects -- you
may remember some IDs that you only did after the restored save,
but you may also forget whether you got certain resistances before
or after the save. In any case the effects are a lot smaller than
losing
your entire game due to a crash. (Honestly I think it'd be nice if the
program deleted the save file when you exited, due to dying or saving,
rather than when you started up; that'd be like an automatic backup
in case of crashes.)

Anyway, congratulations!


